# Layout

Broker-specific code and output go in `brokers/<broker>/`. Shared facts about the market stay out of broker folders: order books in `spreads/`, taxes and catalogues at the repo root.

- Scrapers (`*_scraping.mjs`), probes, cost scripts, experiments, `<broker>-parsed.json`, and `logo.png` live in `brokers/<broker>/`. Never leave a copy of a scraper at the root or directly under `brokers/`.
- Spread scripts and their JSON live in `spreads/` (`spread.mjs`, `venues.mjs`, `gulf.mjs`, `rule606.mjs`, `rule605-monthly.mjs`, `xlm.mjs`, `xlm-monthly.mjs`, the `*-touch.mjs` readers, `spread.json`, the touch files, Rule 605/606). `taxes.mjs`, `taxMap.mjs`, `catalogues.mjs`, and `front.mjs` / `front.html` stay at the root. Instrument lists and prices live in `assets/` (`ETF_list.py`, `Stock_list.py`, `Crypto_list.py`, `etfs.csv`, `stocks.csv`, `cryptos.csv`, `prices.mjs`, `prices.json`).
- `taxes.json` stays at the root, next to `taxes.mjs`. It is keyed by ISIN (`byIsin`) for every `*_cost.mjs`; `byCode` is only the Trading212 sweep. A catalogue belongs in its broker folder. From a broker script the spread file is `../../spreads/spread.json`.
- A tax or spread sourced from one broker still belongs with the shared files if every other broker can use the figure: taxes at the root, order books in `spreads/`. The tax reader may sit at the root even when it talks to Trading212.
- From a broker script, shared files are `../../assets/etfs.csv` (via `import.meta.url`), not a root-relative path that only works if cwd is the repo.
